      "justification": "vulnerable_code_not_in_execute_path",
      "impact_statement": "The flaw is in mount(8)'s X-mount.* helper/post-hook handling and needs a privileged (SUID or root) mount invocation. The mount package is purged from the image; As deployed by the chart the container runs as uid 10001 with all capabilities dropped and a read-only root filesystem (containerSecurityContext), and the only processes it starts are its own Python entrypoints, so libmount's mount context is never driven."
